      "Data Quality" : {
        "Geospatial Resolution" : "National, State",
        "Footnotes" : "National estimates for retail pharmacies and physicians’ medical offices include vaccinations administered in 50 states and DC. National estimates for these medical office vaccinations do not include doses where geographic information (i.e. which state the dose was administered in) was missing. Pharmacy data are through Friday of each week and medical office data are through Saturday of each week. More information about IQVIA can be found here: (https://www.iqvia.com/insights/the-iqvia-institute/available-iqvia-data). Week ending dates for prior seasons are aligned to most closely match the current season's week ending dates. King, L. M., Bartoces, M., Fleming-Dutra, K. E., et al. (2020). Changes in US outpatient antibiotic prescriptions from 2011–2016. Clinical Infectious Diseases, 70(3), 370-377 (https://academic.oup.com/cid/article/70/3/370/5382371). McLaughlin, J. M., Swerdlow, D. L., Khan, F., et al. (2019). Disparities in uptake of 13-valent pneumococcal conjugate vaccine among older adults in the United States. Human vaccines & immunotherapeutics, 15(4), 841-849 https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/21645515.2018.1564434. Using the raw number of doses administered at a subset of retail pharmacies, IQVIA uses a proprietary projection methodology to estimate the projected number of vaccinations administered at all retail pharmacies. For the 2024–25 season, projected estimates were based on a subset of 41,214 pharmacies. The total number of retail pharmacies in the U.S. was estimated at 57,000 in 2022 (The retail pharmacy of the future | McKinsey. https://www.mckinsey.com/industries/healthcare/our-insights/meeting-changing-consumer-needs-the-us-retail-pharmacy-of-the-future, Accessed on 08.21.2025). The estimates include flu vaccinations that were billed to insurers (i.e. claims) or paid by cash. Projected pharmacy estimates are updated each week for the prior 13 weeks but an initial evaluation has shown that the number of doses changed minimally over time. Using the raw number of doses administered at the offices of a subset of physicians from American Medical Association (AMA) proprietary list, IQVIA uses a proprietary projection methodology to estimate the projected number of vaccinations administered in medical offices of all physicians from AMA’s list. For the 2024–25 season, projected estimates were based on a subset of 67,545 AMA office-based physicians who administered flu vaccine. For context, for 2022–23, the number of office-based physicians in the U.S. is 691,382 (https://data.hrsa.gov/topics/health-workforce/nchwa/ahrf). The number of AMA primary care physicians in the U.S. is 258,350. Total number of physicians of all specialties is 989,320; of these, primary care physicians include Internal Medicine (IM), Family Medicine/General Practice, IM/Pediatrics, and Geriatrics (U.S. Physician Workforce Data Dashboard | AAMC at https://www.aamc.org/data-reports/report/us-physician-workforce-data-dashboard). The estimates include flu vaccinations that are claims-based only, and estimates are expected to increase over time for a given time period as claims are processed and adjudicated. Projected estimates are updated monthly and do not mature until about two months. This results in an increase or decrease in the initial or subsequent estimates for a given week (up to ~10% based on initial evaluations). As an example, the estimate for week ending August 27, 2022, was 198,401 when it was first reported and increased (10.7%) to 219,558 week ending October 8, 2022, and remained unchanged thereafter through the end of the flu season as of the week ending May 27, 2023. Archived data are available here: (https://data.cdc.gov/resource/uxgd-cqqc).",
        "Suggested Citation" : "National Center for Immunization and Respiratory Diseases, U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. Weekly Cumulative Number of Influenza Vaccinations Administered in Retail Pharmacies and Physicians’ Medical Offices, by Influenza Season and Age Group, Adults 18 years and older, United States. "
